Third-party components
======================

Nothing in this list is redistributed here. They are named in
main/idf_component.yml and fetched at build time by the ESP-IDF component
manager, so what you get comes from upstream. This file is a map of what the
firmware pulls in and under what terms.

  ESP-IDF                Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  LVGL 9.5               MIT             LVGL Kft.
  TinyUSB                MIT             Ha Thach and contributors
  esp_lvgl_adapter       Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  esp_lcd_co5300         Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  esp_codec_dev          Apache-2.0      Espressif Systems
  esp32_s3_touch_amoled_1_75c            Waveshare (board support)
  esp_lcd_touch_cst9217                  Waveshare (touch driver)
  qmi8658                                Waveshare (IMU driver)

Fonts
-----
The UI uses Montserrat, which ships inside LVGL under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. No font files are added by this repository.

The clock face draws its digits as seven-segment shapes rather than glyphs,
so it needs no font at all.

Artwork
-------
Every image in main/assets/ is generated by tools/mkassets.py from the
simulator's own screenshots, or drawn by that script. The home background and
both clock faces are drawn at runtime in code. Each planet is drawn in code too
(main/apps/orb.c) whenever its map below is absent.

The four planet maps in main/assets/orb_tex_*.h are the exception, and they
are listed under Imagery below. Replace or delete them freely — orb.c uses
whichever of them is present and falls back to drawing the planet itself, so
removing a file costs a picture and breaks nothing.

Imagery
-------
The planet maps are NASA imagery, baked to 512x256 RGB565 by
tools/make-orb-texture.py. NASA content is generally not subject to copyright
in the United States; each source below was checked for a third-party
copyright holder in its caption and none carries one. Credit is given because
NASA asks for it, not because the licence compels it.

  main/assets/orb_tex_moon.h
    CGI Moon Kit, LROC Hapke-normalised WAC mosaic (lroc_color_poles_2k)
    NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio · https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4720
    Visualizer Ernie Wright (USRA), scientist Noah Petro (NASA/GSFC)

  main/assets/orb_tex_earth.h
    Blue Marble Next Generation with topography and bathymetry, December 2004
    NASA Earth Observatory · https://visibleearth.nasa.gov/images/73909

  main/assets/orb_tex_jupiter.h
    PIA07782, Cassini's best maps of Jupiter (cylindrical)
    NASA/JPL/Space Science Institute
    https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/images/pia07782-cassinis-best-maps-of-jupiter-cylindrical-map/

  main/assets/orb_tex_sun.h
    Full map of the Sun's surface, 304 Angstrom, STEREO EUVI and SDO AIA
    NASA JPL · https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/30362/

Neither NASA nor JPL endorses this project. Nothing here uses the NASA
insignia or logotype, which are protected separately.
